    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-upside slate today, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (78.29) and **Yordan Alvarez** (72.69). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play; he benefits from a generous matchup against Taj Bradley and, crucially, faces a battery that allows stolen bases, perfectly aligning with our organizational mandate to capitalize on speed. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite facing a left-on-left matchup against Trevor Rogers; his elite xwOBA of .475 overrides any platoon concerns, as his power-production floor is simply too high to leave on the pine. **Colt Keith** (69.64) and **Junior Caminero** (66.95) also project strongly, bolstered by favorable park factors and the \"Wind Out\" condition in **Junior Caminero**\u2019s game, which should provide a lift to his power output.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Chase Meidroth** (52.83). While his matchup against Shane Bieber is statistically favorable given Bieber\u2019s 5.51 xERA, his projected spot at the bottom of the order heavily depressed his score compared to the aggressive top-of-the-order placement for **Lars Nootbaar** (63.99) and **Christian Yelich** (62.43). We are leaning into the volume of plate appearances at the top of the lineup today, prioritizing **Trea Turner** (65.78) and his 10% order bonus over the marginal utility of our bench depth. Note that all scores are currently based on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions; **Dillon Dingler** (51.06) and **Gary Sanchez** (44.31) are currently our riskiest starts due to defensive/platoon variability. Should any official lineup shifts move our core hitters down the order, we will need to re-evaluate the impact on our daily efficiency.",
